<title>USA: TABLE-T R Financial Q2 shr $0.48 vs $0.41.</title>
<headline>TABLE-T R Financial Q2 shr $0.48 vs $0.41.</headline>
<dateline>GARDEN CITY, N.Y. 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>T R Financial Corp  and subsidiaries</p>
<p>			    Consolidated statements of income</p>
<p>					   (Unaudited)</p>
<p>			     Three months ended     Six months ended</p>
<p>					   June 30,		 June 30,</p>
<p>				    1997     1996	  1997     1996</p>
<p>			    (in thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>Interest income:</p>
<p>Mortgage loans	    $32,176  $27,732	$62,642  $53,800</p>
<p>Mortgage-backed</p>
<p>securities		   21,432   18,972	 41,763   37,344</p>
<p>Bonds, equities and</p>
<p>other investments	   7,433    5,617	 13,971   11,883</p>
<p>Other loans		   2,083    1,599	  4,205    3,051</p>
<p>Total interest income    63,124   53,920	122,581  106,078</p>
<p>Total non-interest income 2,986    3,808	  5,966    8,428</p>
<p>Net income		   $8,414   $7,214	$16,178  $14,398</p>
<p>Income per common and</p>
<p>common equivalent share   $0.48    $0.41	  $0.92    $0.81</p>
<p>SOURCE:  T R Financial Corp.</p>
<p>NOTE: The bank had $3.55 billion in assets as of June 30 1997, compared with $3.26 billion as of December 31 1996.</p>
</text>
